,"p_yest":"The high of <strong>54\u00b0F</strong> was typical for November 13. The normal high for the date is 54\u00b0F, and the record is 71\u00b0F (1999). The low of <strong>45\u00b0F</strong> was the 24th warmest November 13 low (tied) of 132 since 1894.","t_rec":"Record highs and lows, by the decade that set them","p_rec":"If Eugene's climate weren't changing, every year would have the same chance of holding a daily record. Since 2000, Eugene has set <strong>64 standing record lows</strong>, close to the 75 that chance alone would give, and <strong>99 record highs</strong>, more than the 75 that chance alone would give. The 2020s hold the most record highs of any decade (43). Eugene's all-time high is 111\u00b0F, on June 27, 2021.","t_chg":"Eugene's days got warmer. Its nights didn't.","p_chg":"Across 125 complete years: Eugene's average low shows no clear change: +0.04\u00b0F per decade, a range (\u22120.02 to +0.10) that includes zero. Eugene's average high has risen <strong class='sig'>+0.14\u00b0F per decade</strong> (95% range +0.08 to +0.21), about +1.8\u00b0F since 1896.","t_mon":"Lows rose in 3 of 12 months. Highs rose in 6 of 12 months.","t_rain":"Rain and snow: no clear long-term change","p_rain":"Eugene's yearly precipitation shows no clear long-term change (+0.32 inches per decade, a range that includes zero). The 1991\u20132020 normal is 40.8 inches a year. The wettest year was 1996 (76.51 in); the driest, 2013 (21.19 in).","show_snow":true,"sig_bars":{"lo":false,"hi":false},"t_year":"2026 so far: 9 daily record highs, 1 daily record low"}}